      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "The same general procedure was used for both complexes. LH2 (0.04 g, 0.26 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was treated with LnCl3·nH2O (0.07 g, 0.26 mmol) and stirred for about 0.5 h. Triethylamine (0.14 mL, four molar equivalents) and 1,1,1-trifluoroacetylacetone (0.03 mL, 0.16 mmol) were added. The clear orange-yellow solution was stirred for 6 h at room temperature, concentrated, and the solid residue was washed with diethyl ether, dried in air, and dissolved in MeOH/CHCl3 (10 mL/10 mL, v/v). The filtered yellow solution was left to crystallize, giving orange needle crystals suitable for X-ray diffraction within 10 days. For 1 the metal salt was DyCl3·6H2O.",
